From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nabeel Sowan <nabeel@vibes.se>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 11:32:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/13] feature: power the internal display off on lid close,
 split from lock

Turning the display off, locking, and suspending are three separate
concerns on lid close, and they were tangled. The inhibit gate and the
docked-ignore path both returned early doing nothing, so under a shut lid
the internal panel stayed lit in exactly the two modes a user reaches for
when stowing the machine running. forceDpmsOffOnLidClose did blank the
display, but only in the undocked lock path, and through xset dpms force
off -- which is global, so it could never be used docked without blanking
the external too.

Power the internal panel off as its own step, run first and
unconditionally on lid close while the session is active, before the
inhibit gate and independent of lock, suspend and the docked policy. A
shut lid is never being looked at, so this is the one lid-close response
that is always wanted. powerSaveInternalDisplay() picks the mechanism and
records what it did so the open path undoes exactly that:

  - docked (an external display is driving): disable the internal output
    entirely, light and drive both, external untouched;
  - alone (the internal panel is the only display): force DPMS off, a
    power state rather than a configuration change, so no zero-display
    moment, restoring on the next input event -- global DPMS is safe here
    because there is no external to blank;
  - lidDisplayLightOnly: dim the backlight to nothing and change no
    display configuration or power state, for setups that cannot take an
    output being reconfigured or a transient zero-display state.

Add the lidDisplayLightOnly config key (default off) for the last case.
Make forceDpmsOffOnLidClose the single master enable for all of the
above, default on -- the name is now historical but kept so existing
configs and an existing =false opt-out still read. Retire
switchOffPanelOnLidClose, folded into the master, and gate the startup
panel-heal on the master too. The two stray forceDPMSOff() calls in the
lock branches are gone, which also removes the docked case where the
global DPMS call would have blanked the external.

Signed-off-by: Nabeel Sowan <nabeel@vibes.se>
